    <div class="tg-hero__inner">
      <span class="tg-hero__type">Part I of Five</span>
      <h1 class="tg-hero__title">The Thread from Eden to the New Covenant</h1>
      <p class="tg-hero__intro">
        The question of assurance is usually argued out of a dozen New Testament
        verses, as though the problem began with Paul. It did not. Every element of
        the debate — free rescue, covenant obligation, real apostasy, a preserved
        remnant, a heart God himself changes — is already present in the Hebrew
        Scriptures, in the same tension, often in the same book. This part follows
        the thread from Eden to Malachi and asks what has been required of the saved
        person from the beginning.
      </p>
      <blockquote class="tg-hero__key-verse">
        <p>And he believed the LORD, and he counted it to him as righteousness.</p>
        <cite><a class="ref" data-ref="Genesis 15:6">Genesis 15:6</a></cite>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </header><main>
